  "methodology": "Other",
  "methodology_other": "The product is based on in-situ rain gauge measurements that undergo strict quality\ncontrol and are interpolated onto a regular grid. It distinguishes itself by using\nthe largest available database of station data, making it one of the most reliable\ngridded precipitation datasets for land areas.",
  "name": "acmad-gpcc-monthly-precipitation",
  "notes": "The Global Precipitation Climatology Centre (GPCC) Monthly Precipitation dataset provides\ngridded gauge-analysis products focusing on land-surface precipitation. This dataset\nserves as a high-quality observational baseline for climate monitoring across Africa.\nIt is constructed from quality-controlled data from thousands of rain gauges worldwide.\n\n\nAt ACMAD, this data often serves as the \"truth\" or reference layer for calibrating\nsatellite estimates and for calculating long-term indices like SPI. It is critical\nfor retrospective analysis, model verification, and understanding the climatological\ncontext of current weather events.",
  "num_resources": 18,
  "num_tags": 4,
  "organization": {
    "id": "2dbc5dcc-1507-470b-a414-0687e0980ecb",
    "name": "acmad",
    "title": "African Center of Meteorological Applications for Development",
    "type": "organization",
    "description": "ACMAD was created through **Resolution 540** of the **UNECA Conference of Ministers** in **April 1985**, following the severe droughts of the 1970s and 1980s, **ACMAD** was established in **Niamey, Niger** in **October 1992** with two mandates:\r\n\r\n- **Continental Weather and Climate Watch Centre for Africa**  \r\n   Monitoring, forecasting, and early warning for droughts, floods, tropical cyclones, and other extreme events. In this regard, ACMAD became:\r\n\r\n       +  The Continental Climate Watch Centre was achieved with ACMAD designated by the WMO Congress after a successful demonstration phase as a Regional Climate Centre for Africa in May 2015.\r\n\r\n       +  The Continental Weather Watch Centre was achieved with the Continental Multi-Hazards Advisory Centre inaugurated in November 2022, and ACMAD is providing contributions to continental watches and disaster situation reports to support the situation room operations at the African Union Commission Headquarters in Addis Ababa.\r\n\r\n- **Institution of excellence for the application of meteorology for sustainable development**\r\nThis includes capacity building, development of methods, tools and products, contributions to global weather and climate programs, database development, and research and innovation as functions.\r\n\r\nSince **July 2024**, ACMAD has been a member of the **NoE (Africa Network of Excellence for DRR)**.\r\n\r\n   **ACMAD Provides the following Bulletins with Continental coverage:** <ul>\r\n<li>Impact-based Forecast Bulletin</li>\r\n<li>Multi-Hazard Bulletin</li> \r\n<li>Seasonal Climate Forecast Bulletin</li> \r\n<li>Monthly Climate Bulletin</li>\r\n</ul>  \r\n\r\n The bulletins are in PDF format  and are are available on the website: https://www.acmad.org  \r\n   * API for the Drought: https://ada.acmad.org/api",
